WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:01.942
Oh, hello there, I'm Gav.

00:00:01.942 --> 00:00:03.760
Oh, hello, I'm Dan.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:04.593
Oh, hello.

00:00:04.593 --> 00:00:06.490
We're the Slow Mo Guys.

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:07.323
We're sat down.

00:00:07.323 --> 00:00:09.500
Take a seat yourself, if you want.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:10.440
No need to stand.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:11.730
Why would they be stood
there on the computer?

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:15.011
Like, as soon as they're
like, oh, Slow Mo Guys video.

00:00:15.011 --> 00:00:16.600
Just stand up to watch this.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.450
Few months ago, we were very kindly given

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.250
this car by Traxxas.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:22.670
It goes 100 miles an hour.

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:23.503
Beast.

00:00:23.503 --> 00:00:25.150
We used it 'cause it was the fastest car

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:26.760
I could find on the internet,

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.620
and we had a problem
when we were filming it

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:33.330
in that the audio was
too good, crystal clear,

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:36.510
sort of so good that it
hurt your ears to listen to.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:37.530
Often the case on a Slow Mo Guys video.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:38.363
Often the case.

00:00:38.363 --> 00:00:39.500
Here's an example of it.

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:46.923
See what I mean?

00:00:46.923 --> 00:00:47.756
Yeah, very clear.

00:00:47.756 --> 00:00:48.589
Sounds very clear.

00:00:48.589 --> 00:00:50.840
So what we're gonna do is
make a new intro for you

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:53.100
that is worse sounding.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.440
First thing we thought we'd
do is test out the speed

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.760
by driving it at myself
at 100 miles an hour.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.390
I thought, wouldn't it be cool

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:04.470
if you could jump over a
100 mile an hour object

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:05.960
coming straight at your own legs?

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:06.970
I was like, yeah.

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:09.640
So, wait, I have to drive
it at myself and jump?

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:11.590
And then you're like, also do a 180,

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:13.443
so I had to jump,
turn in the air,

00:01:13.443 --> 00:01:15.535
still controlling the
car, at 100 miles an hour.

00:01:21.193 --> 00:01:22.026
Woo.

00:01:23.593 --> 00:01:24.974
Was that scary?

00:01:24.974 --> 00:01:26.037
It's pretty weird.

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:55.230
Next, we decided, what
would a crash look like?

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:56.560
Little off-road spill,

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:59.360
so Dan drove the car from the flat tarmac

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:01.760
onto the grass, and I
tracked it in high speed.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:02.914
This is what it looked like.

00:02:07.322 --> 00:02:08.155
Oh.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:54.530
Serious James Bond flips there.

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:55.730
It looked pretty cool.
Yeah, kicked up the grass,

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:56.563
flying through the air.

00:02:56.563 --> 00:02:58.150
I've done it in real
life, and let me tell you,

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:00.210
it's better to watch it when
it's a remote control car,

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:01.440
not you in the car.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:02.910
Fiddling with the radio, weren't you?

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:05.080
Yeah, I told people there was an animal

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:05.913
and I swerved to avoid it,

00:03:05.913 --> 00:03:07.680
but I was literally just
playing with the radio,

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:08.513
not paying attention,

00:03:08.513 --> 00:03:10.000
and I span it backwards into a bush.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:10.833
Well done there.

00:03:10.833 --> 00:03:11.666
Yep, good work.

00:03:11.666 --> 00:03:13.020
Next up, we thought it'd be a good idea

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:15.900
to pour a lump of flour on the road

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:18.710
and have it drive either
over it or through it.

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:21.580
Either way, the particles
of flour should look cool.

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:25.100
Okay, so, to help show
the speed of this car,

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.500
I'm gonna plunk down an
entire bag of flour here

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:32.390
and watch it get obliterated in slow mo.

00:03:37.051 --> 00:03:37.884
Oh.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.290
We were actually mainly out there

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.170
filming the flamethrower video,

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:38.700
of which all of the
audio is fine, somehow.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:39.810
The wind must've kicked up

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:40.920
while we were doing this one,

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.020
so you suited up again,

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:45.067
and we drove the car through the flames.

00:06:02.277 --> 00:06:03.850
So, at this point,

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:05.760
we haven't broken this thing yet, somehow,

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:08.670
so I felt like the finale was clear.

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:09.630
Just get another one.

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:11.160
Get a second one of these bad boys.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:12.500
This one's all see-through, obviously,

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:14.240
so we can see the individual bits

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.170
when it crashes into this one.

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:18.463
We went for a head-on collision.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:26.954
Oh.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:07:00.100
Aw, that wheel is wedged up there.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:00.933
Is it in the car?

00:07:00.933 --> 00:07:02.420
Yeah, it's, like, shoved up inside.

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:04.090
My beauty.

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:06.590
So when we were filming that, I thought,

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:08.290
little bit wasteful, what we did there.

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:10.960
Sort of very high performance
remote control cars,

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:12.590
definitely for enthusiasts.

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:13.423
Yeah.

00:07:13.423 --> 00:07:15.350
But I've gotta say, whenever
I see a remote control car,

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:17.440
I always think, what would it look like

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:18.600
if two slammed into each other?

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:20.600
I know that people that
want one of these cars

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:22.160
and use these cars would be like,

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:23.630
oh, I really want to crash one into it,

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:25.170
but I just can't do it, 'cause it's mine.

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:26.350
It's my piece of kit.
It would be,

00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:27.450
I really want to crash one.

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:28.560
I don't want to crash mine.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:29.393
Yeah, yeah.

00:07:29.393 --> 00:07:30.700
We've done it for you in slow motion.

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:32.180
Yeah, so it is wasteful,

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.590
but now you don't have to experiment

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:34.700
and damage your own goods,

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:36.304
if you were thinking of it.

00:07:36.304 --> 00:07:37.970
Probably weren't, but.
Worth it. Worth it.

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:39.950
I don't know, I'm always
fascinated by destruction.

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:43.000
A big, wet thanks to Traxxas

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:44.590
for giving us two free cars,

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:45.940
and then repairing them for us.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:47.221
They put them into the GTA garage,

00:07:47.221 --> 00:07:48.910
and moved it back out,
and that's all it...

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:50.490
Straight in and out.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:53.320
Very much appreciate it
for the use of this video,

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:56.283
and hopefully, you got some
enjoyment out of it too.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:59.340
Feel free to follow us on Twitter,

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:01.580
buy some smerch, and...

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:03.030
Second channel?

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:04.430
So this is second channel too.

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:05.263
Yep.

